<title>SWITZERLAND: SIG sees higher 1996, 1997 profits.</title>
<headline>SIG sees higher 1996, 1997 profits.</headline>
<dateline>NEUHAUSEN, Switzerland 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss mechanical engineering group SIG said it expected 1996 net profit to increase from 1995's 70.1 million Swiss francs and saw further improvement in 1997.</p>
<p>SIG said it also expected operating profit to rise in 1996 and 1997 from 102.3 million Swiss francs in 1995. Sales this year were seen growing from a 1996 total of 1,638 million reported earlier.</p>
<p>The company's full name is SIG Schweizerische Industrie-Gesellschaft Holding AG.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Newsroom, +41-1-631 7340</p>
